    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Source-record read gate as an endpoint filter" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter.cs">
        The quick-create route already gates its caller-supplied source id this way. Mirror the shape rather than inventing a second mechanism.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <justification>
    <existing>`QuickCreateSourceAccessFilter.cs` — the same gate for the quick-create route.</existing>
    <extension>The existing filter is bound to quick-create's request shape and single source id; `/todo` has four ids across three carrier types. Extend if the existing filter generalises cleanly; otherwise mirror it. Decide by reading it, and record which was done.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any authenticated user confirms the existence of arbitrary invoice, document and communication GUIDs, harvests their parent matter ids, and attaches their own To Dos to records they cannot read — which FR-26 inheritance then shows to that record's members.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

